meta {
  name: Notifications
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/method/implementor.client_api.get_notifications?unread_only=1&limit=4
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  unread_only: 1
  limit: 4
  ~customer: Hamza
}

tests {
  test("returns 200", function () {
    expect(res.status).to.equal(200);
  });
  
  test("has message", function () {
    expect(res.body).to.have.property("message");
  });

  test("returns unread notifications with the documented fields", function () {
    const list = res.body.message;
    expect(list).to.be.an("array");
    expect(list.length).to.be.at.most(4);
    list.forEach(function (n) {
      ["name", "kind", "subject", "document_type", "document_name", "read", "creation"].forEach(function (k) {
        expect(n).to.have.property(k);
      });
      expect(n.read).to.equal(0);
    });
  });
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Lists the user's notifications.
  
  **Endpoint:** `GET /api/method/implementor.client_api.get_notifications`  
  **Screen:** Notifications
  
  **Permission:** Signed-in user linked to a client company. Returns the notifications addressed to the signed-in user (not filtered by company).

  **Method:** GET. The server does not refuse a POST, but use GET.

  **Query parameters:**

  | Field | Type | Required | Example | Notes |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `unread_only` | 0 / 1 | no | `1` | Default `0` (all). `1` returns only unread ones. |
  | `limit` | int | no | `4` | Default `30`, maximum `100`. `0` or an invalid value means 30. |
  | `customer` | string | no | `Hamza` | Not used by the app. The server picks the user's company. Disabled by default. |

  **Response:** a list, newest first. No paging beyond `limit`.

  ```json
  {
    "message": [
      {
        "name": "bbjqcbg636",
        "kind": "action_assigned",
        "subject": "Upload VAT registration certificate (due 23-11-2026)",
        "document_type": "ToDo",
        "document_name": "ee1p51uomd",
        "read": 0,
        "creation": "2026-11-06 09:30:12.345678"
      }
    ]
  }
  ```

  **Field notes:**

  - `kind`: what the notification is about, so the app can pick the icon and the screen to open. One of the codes below, or `null` for older and system notifications (open nothing special, just show `subject`).

    | `kind` | Sent when | Sent to | `document_type` / `document_name` | Open |
    | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
    | `ticket_waiting_on_client` | Our team sets the ticket to Waiting on Client | Ticket raiser | `Support Ticket` / ticket ID | Ticket detail |
    | `ticket_resolved` | Our team marks the ticket Resolved | Ticket raiser | `Support Ticket` / ticket ID | Ticket detail (confirm fix + rate) |
    | `ticket_status_changed` | Our team changes the ticket to any other status | Ticket raiser | `Support Ticket` / ticket ID | Ticket detail |
    | `ticket_reply` | Our team comments on the ticket | Ticket raiser | `Support Ticket` / ticket ID | Ticket detail |
    | `action_assigned` | An action (to-do) is assigned to the user | That user | `ToDo` / action ID | Actions |
    | `action_due_soon` | Daily, 8 AM: an open action is due tomorrow | That user | `ToDo` / action ID | Actions |
    | `action_overdue` | Daily, 8 AM: an open action was due yesterday | That user | `ToDo` / action ID | Actions |
    | `milestone_ready` | A milestone becomes ready for sign-off | The company's Client Admins | `Project` / project ID | Project → Milestones |
    | `project_status_changed` | The project status changes (e.g. Active → Go-Live) | All the company's client users | `Project` / project ID | Project |
    | `payment_due` | A milestone's payment is set to Pending | The company's Client Admins | `Project` / project ID | Project → Milestones |
    | `payment_overdue` | A milestone's payment is set to Overdue | The company's Client Admins | `Project` / project ID | Project → Milestones |
    | `amc_expiring` | Daily, 8 AM: the AMC ends in 30 or 7 days | The company's Client Admins | `Project` / project ID | AMC |
    | `amc_expired` | Daily, 8 AM: the AMC ended yesterday | The company's Client Admins | `Project` / project ID | AMC |
    | `server_down` | The 5-minute status check finds the server Offline | All the company's client users | `Server` / server ID | Server detail |
    | `server_up` | The server is Online again after being Offline | All the company's client users | `Server` / server ID | Server detail |
    | `backup_overdue` | No confirmed backup in the last 26 hours | All the company's client users | `Server` / server ID | Backups |
    | `backup_failed` | The newest backup run failed | All the company's client users | `Server` / server ID | Backups |
    | `training_scheduled` | A training session is added or its time changes | All the company's client users | `Training Session` / session ID | Project → Training |
    | `training_reminder` | Daily, 8 AM: a training session is tomorrow | All the company's client users | `Training Session` / session ID | Project → Training |

    The user is never notified about their own actions (their own comment, status change or sign-off). Server and backup notifications are sent once when the state changes, not on every check. Daily ones are sent at most once a day per record. Server, backup and daily checks use the Asia/Riyadh time zone.
  - `subject`: ready-to-show text in English, e.g. `Ticket ST-0012: Login issue is waiting for your reply.`
  - `document_type` / `document_name`: the record the notification is about (e.g. `Support Ticket` + ticket ID, `ToDo` + action ID). Either can be null.
  - `read`: integer `0` (unread) or `1` (read), not a boolean.
  - `creation`: server format **without** an offset (`YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS.ffffff`, server time zone), not ISO 8601. Not converted yet.

  **Push notifications:** every notification with a `kind` is also sent as a Firebase push to the device token on the user's Employee record. The push `data` carries strings only:

  ```json
  {
    "type": "notification",
    "screen": "Notification",
    "kind": "ticket_reply",
    "notification": "bbjqcbg636",
    "document_type": "Support Ticket",
    "document_name": "q4sf1md4lh"
  }
  ```

  `notification` is the `name` above, so the app can call **Mark read** when the push is tapped.

  **Errors:**

  - **401** (no error_code): token expired or invalid. Refresh once and retry, else sign out.
  - **403** (no error_code): no Authorization header sent.
  - **403** `no_client_linked`: the user isn't linked to any client company.
  - **403** `not_permitted`: `customer` was sent and isn't the user's company.
}
